Let VectCutAPI import on Python 3.9 (macOS system/Xcode Python).

VectCutAPI declares requires-python = ">=3.10" and `add_text_impl.py` uses PEP
604 annotations (`draft_id: str | None = None`). On Python 3.9 those are valid
syntax but fail when the annotation is EVALUATED at import time:

    TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'type' and 'NoneType'

macOS ships Python 3.9 (and Xcode's python3 is 3.9), so `python3
capcut_server.py` fails before the server starts.

`from __future__ import annotations` makes every annotation in the module a
lazily-evaluated string, which is exactly what PEP 604 needs on 3.9. An AST scan
of the whole repository -- capcut_server.py, every *_impl.py, and all of
pyJianYingDraft -- found PEP 604 unions in runtime-evaluated positions in this
one file only (6 parameter annotations), and no other 3.10-only syntax such as
match statements. Nothing in this module inspects __annotations__ at runtime, so
turning them into strings changes no behaviour.

This is a workaround, not a supported configuration: upstream targets 3.10+, so
a future VectCutAPI update may reintroduce 3.10-only code. The durable fix is to
run it on Python 3.11:

    brew install python@3.11
    python3.11 -m pip install -r requirements-pinned.txt
    python3.11 capcut_server.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9000

Apply with:
    cd /path/to/VectCutAPI
    git apply /path/to/capcut-mcp-server/vectcutapi/python39-compat.patch

diff --git a/add_text_impl.py b/add_text_impl.py
--- a/add_text_impl.py
+++ b/add_text_impl.py
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+from __future__ import annotations  # keep PEP 604 annotations lazy (Python 3.9)
+
 import pyJianYingDraft as draft
 from settings.local import IS_CAPCUT_ENV
 from util import generate_draft_url, hex_to_rgb
